WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Good evening.

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope you're all
doing well tonight.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now I would like to
get to the news.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:10.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
The CDC announced last wee
that fully vaccinated American

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.112 line:92%
no longer need to wear masks

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
in most indoor
or outdoor settings.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my God, finally!",
said unvaccinated Americans.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
After the CDC
announced it on Thursday

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:24.290
that vaccinated people no longer
need to wear face masks indoors,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
said that masks

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
will still be required
in the chamber.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when Marjorie Taylor Green
heard that,

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:35.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
she became so unhinged
that nobody noticed

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
any change in
her demeanor whatsoever.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
According to
"The New York Times,"

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Biden
does not make quick decision

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
and often asks for
detailed briefings and debates

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
from staffers
before making up his mind,

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:50.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is honestly refreshing
considering the last guy

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:54.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
didn't always get
the wrapper off the burger

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.088 size:88% position:44% line:92%
According to a new poll,

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:58.491 size:84% position:42%
only 52% of Americans
say they trust the CDC.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:02.595
Reached for comment,
the CDC said, "Ask again later."

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
According to a new report in
"The New York Times,"

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.333
First Lady Dr. Jill Biden
is a wine connoisseur.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dr. Biden first
became interested in wine

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
the 38th time
she heard about Scranton.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm just going to
top this off."

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
According to a new survey,
72% of Americans

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
think they could beat a ra
in a fight.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
9% think they could beat
a crocodile.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
And 6% think they could beat
a grizzly bear.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
This news first reported
by the kid

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.290 line:92%
you're trying to get to bed.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't know.
Uh, I guess rat, yes.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Crocodile, maybe."

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
Researchers in Japan
recently found that mammal

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have been deprived
of air can be saved

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
by receiving oxygen
through their anuses.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
While researchers deprived
of oxygen

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:49.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
come up with
some pretty wild stuff.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:52.812
A 111-year-old man in Australia,
who is believed to be

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
the country's oldest-ever man,
said in a recent interview

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:59.586
that the secret to living a long
life is eating chicken brains.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:05.391
Oh, I didn't even know you could
get Hot Pockets in Australia

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, finally,
today was National Walnut Day.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:11.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
Celebrate by ruining
some chocolate-chip cookies.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was the monologue,
everybody.

